# phi-agent — coding perimeter.
#
# Grammar: see the header of ~/.local/bin/phi-agent-contain.
# Coding has a shell; the containment IS the boundary. Network is removed
# (--unshare-net) and reintroduced as a whitelist by phi-agent-contain; there
# is no direct route out of this namespace. The workdir — the one directory
# the session can write to — and the net bridge dir are bound by
# phi-agent-contain itself, not here: both are chosen or created per
# session, not a fixed perimeter path.
#
# Git identity is passed as GIT_AUTHOR_* / GIT_COMMITTER_* environment
# variables, never by mounting ~/.gitconfig (which can carry credential
# helpers and insteadOf URL rewrites). Coding does not publish to or fetch
# from remotes: it edits and commits locally; publishing is the user's
# action. No SSH key, no SSH-agent socket, and no network path to a forge.

# Per-profile cache — writable.
rw   @AGENT_CACHE@               @CONTAINER_HOME@/.cache

# Toolchain caches (cargo, go, npm, ...) dedicated to coding, separate from
# the user's own. Path from PHI_AGENT_A2_TOOLCHAIN_CACHE, default under
# coding's own cache tree.
rw?  @A2_TOOLCHAIN_CACHE@        @CONTAINER_HOME@/.cache/phi-agent-toolchains
